    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105422",
      "sequence": 6,
      "source_sequence": 6,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Visual bias in the Brexit referendum: A quantitative analysis of newspaper images",
      "title_cn": "英国脱欧公投中的视觉偏见：报纸图像的定量分析",
      "authors": [
        "Wanyu Chung",
        "Duiyi Dai",
        "Robert J.R. Elliott"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "In this paper, we investigate whether, and to what extent, UK newspapers exhibited image-based bias in their portrayal of politicians during the 2016 Brexit referendum. We use computer vision and machine learning techniques to first, identify the faces of politicians and assess the emotional content conveyed through their expressions and second, to measure the contextual sentiment of the overall image, including elements such as background, objects, and color. Our findings reveal that tabloid newspapers displayed significant partisan bias. Specifically, pro-leave tabloids were more likely to depict pro-leave politicians with positive facial expressions and in more favorable visual contexts, while pro-remain politicians were portrayed more negatively. This bias was especially pronounced in front-page images and those featuring key political figures, while no comparable patterns were found in broadsheets. However, the visual bias diminished immediately after the referendum vote. Our scalable framework not only provides a systematic way to detect visual bias in political imagery but also underscores the growing need for media accountability and visual literacy as images play an increasingly powerful role in shaping political communication.",
      "abstract_cn": "在本文中，我们调查了英国报纸在2016英国脱欧公投期间对政客的描述是否以及在多大程度上表现出基于图像的偏见。我们使用计算机视觉和机器学习技术来第一识别政客的面孔并评估通过他们的表情传达的情感内容和第二来衡量整个图像的上下文情感，包括背景、物体和颜色等元素。我们的研究结果表明，小报表现出明显的党派偏见。具体来说，支持脱欧的小报更有可能以积极的面部表情和更有利的视觉环境来描绘支持脱欧的政客，而支持留欧的政客则被描绘得更加消极。这种偏见在头版图像和主要政治人物的图像中尤其明显，而在大报中没有发现类似的模式。然而，公投投票后，视觉偏见立即消失。我们的可扩展框架不仅提供了一种系统的方法来检测政治图像中的视觉偏见，而且还强调了对媒体问责和视觉素养日益增长的需求，因为图像在塑造政治传播方面发挥着越来越强大的作用。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105422",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0014292126001662?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
