    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105435",
      "sequence": 10,
      "source_sequence": 10,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Capital reallocation under climate policy uncertainty",
      "title_cn": "气候政策不确定性下的资本重新配置",
      "authors": [
        "Makram Khalil",
        "Felix Strobel"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "In a structural dynamic model that incorporates two broad production sectors with different carbon emissions, we find that climate policy uncertainty (CPU) shocks (i) lower the market value of the highly carbon-emitting sector relative to the low carbon-emitting sector, and (ii) reduce real investment and the capital stock in the highly carbon-emitting sector, while real investment in the sector with low carbon emissions tends to fare better. To apply the theoretical predictions to the data, we employ a news article-based measure of climate policy uncertainty to identify CPU shocks as well as quarterly balance sheet data of listed firms in the United States. In line with the predictions from the theoretical model, we find that in response to CPU shocks (i) financial markets markedly revalue strongly carbon-emitting firms relative to firms with low carbon emissions, and (ii) substantial investment reallocation takes place, in particular from the manufacturing sector towards services.",
      "abstract_cn": "在包含不同碳排放的广泛生产部门的结构动态模型中，我们发现气候政策不确定性（CPU）冲击（i）降低高碳排放部门相对于低碳排放部门的市场价值，以及（ii）减少高碳排放部门的实际投资和资本存量，而低碳排放部门的实际投资往往表现更好。为了将理论预测应用于数据，我们采用基于新闻文章的气候政策不确定性衡量标准来识别 CPU 冲击以及美国上市公司的季度资产负债表数据。根据理论模型的预测，我们发现，为了应对 CPU 冲击，(i) 金融市场明显对碳排放企业相对于低碳排放企业进行重估，并且 (ii) 发生了大量投资重新分配，特别是从制造业转向服务业。",
