    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105423",
      "sequence": 14,
      "source_sequence": 14,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Gender identity and power imbalance in a group contest",
      "title_cn": "团体竞赛中的性别认同和权力失衡",
      "authors": [
        "Defne Mia Aktaş",
        "Florian Heine"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Many high-stakes organisational decisions are made by committees, where members exert costly influence to shape a single collective outcome. When committees are gender-imbalanced, the salience of gender identity may affect who mobilises influence and how numerical power translates into effective decision weight. We study how gender-identity salience interacts with numerical power in a controlled laboratory setting using a group-contest design. We vary the numerical balance of power (Female-Majority vs. Male-Majority) and manipulate whether gender composition is revealed. We find larger, advantaged groups invest significantly more and identity salience has asymmetric effects by gender. Among minority men facing female-majority groups, making gender salient increases investment and their initial disadvantage shrinks over time. Among minority women facing male-majority groups, investment does not increase and their relative disadvantage grows over time. These divergent responses are not explained by general social preferences or in-group cohesion. The findings suggest highlighting gender identity may intensify mobilisation by minority men without similarly empowering minority women, with implications for the design of diversity and transparency policies.",
      "abstract_cn": "许多高风险的组织决策都是由委员会做出的，委员会成员为形成单一的集体结果而施加代价高昂的影响力。当委员会性别不平衡时，性别认同的显着性可能会影响谁调动影响力以及人数权力如何转化为有效的决策权重。我们使用小组竞赛设计，在受控实验室环境中研究性别认同显着性如何与数字力量相互作用。我们改变权力的数量平衡（女性占多数与男性占多数）并操纵是否揭示性别构成。我们发现规模较大、优势群体的投资显着增加，而且身份显着性对性别的影响不对称。在面对女性占多数群体的少数男性中，突出性别会增加投资，并且随着时间的推移，他们最初的劣势会缩小。在面对男性占多数群体的少数女性中，投资并没有增加，而且她们的相对劣势随着时间的推移而增加。这些不同的反应不能用一般社会偏好或群体内凝聚力来解释。研究结果表明，强调性别认同可能会加强少数族裔男性的动员，而不会同样赋予少数族裔女性权力，这会对多样性和透明度政策的设计产生影响。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105423",
