    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.euroecorev.2026.105436",
      "sequence": 15,
      "source_sequence": 15,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "A small volume reduction that melts down the market: Auctions with endogenous rationing",
      "title_cn": "小幅减少导致市场崩溃：内生配给的拍卖",
      "authors": [
        "Karl-Martin Ehrhart",
        "Ann-Katrin Fleck",
        "Marion Ott"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Auctions with endogenous rationing have been introduced to stimulate competition. Such (procurement) auctions reduce the volume put out to tender when competition is low. This paper finds a strong negative effect of endogenous rationing on participation when bid-preparation is costly, counteracting the aim to stimulate competition. For multiple auctioneer's objectives mentioned in directives, we derive optimal mechanisms, which differ due to different evaluation of the tradeoff between participation and bid-preparation costs. Thus, the auctioneer needs to decide on an objective. However, reducing bid-preparation costs improves the optimal values of multiple objective functions.",
      "abstract_cn": "引入内生配给拍卖以刺激竞争。当竞争程度较低时，此类（采购）拍卖会减少招标数量。本文发现，当投标准备成本高昂时，内生配给会对参与产生强烈的负面影响，从而抵消了刺激竞争的目的。对于指令中提到的多个拍卖师的目标，我们得出最佳机制，由于对参与和投标准备成本之间权衡的不同评估而有所不同。因此，拍卖师需要确定一个目标。然而，降低投标准备成本可以提高多个目标函数的最优值。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
